   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hey Rebecca,<div><br></div><div>Unfortunately it is not possible to use TidyLPA to use profiles as predictors of outcomes; however, Mplus is able to do this.  Below is a couple citations for recent articles detailing the various ways to predict outcomes using profiles as predictors in Mplus.</div><div><br></div><div>Asparouhov, T., &amp; Muthén, B. O. (2013). Auxiliary variables in mixture modeling: A 3-step approach using Mplus (Mplus web notes: No. 15). Mplus Web Notes: No. 15, (15), 1–48. <a href=\"https://doi.org/http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2014.915181\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2014.915181&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496030917000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1F17x71v7-FtLGWd0ZcGbx\">https://doi.org/http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2014.915181</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Nylund-Gibson, K., Grimm, R. P., &amp; Masyn, K. E. (2019). Prediction from Latent Classes: A Demonstration of Different Approaches to Include Distal Outcomes in Mixture Models. Structural Equation Modeling, 1–19. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2019.1590146\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2019.1590146&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496030917000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qMf3XUz96v-ExwL385Whl\">https://doi.org/10.1080/10705511.2019.1590146</a><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Jul 10, 2019 at 4:34 PM Rebecca Harmata &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rharma...@sdsu.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
