     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nGood Afternoon,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px;font-size:15px;color:rgb(32,31,30);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-size:12pt;color:black\">I have been transitioning from MPlus to R when estimating latent profiles. I have been searching for syntax in R to see if my\r\n profiles predict workplace outcomes as auxiliary variables, but I am having trouble finding such resources. Is TidyLPA able to do this?</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px;font-size:15px;color:rgb(32,31,30);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-size:12pt;color:black\"> </span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px;font-size:15px;color:rgb(32,31,30);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-size:12pt;color:black\">Thank you for your time!</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><b>Rebecca Harmata</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><b></b>Master&#39;s Student in Psychology</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-to